      "created_at": "2020-06-20T18:24:20Z",
      "updated_at": "2020-06-20T18:24:20Z",
      "body": "The GeoIP database comes in two forms: \"cities\" and \"countries\". It currently uses the Countries database which is about 1.8M (2.4M in the source code), which is a bit large bit still small enough to include in the source code. The Cities version is 29M, which would be >30M in the source code – which is too large IMO. Right now GoatCounter can run without any external dependencies, which is a nice feature I rather like, and I'd rather not lose that. One way to fix that is to create out own GeoDB file with just the data we need, which would vastly reduce the filesize for both cases.\r\n\r\nAnother issue is that we need to be kind-of careful not to record too much specific Personally Identifiable Information (PII). A Country name is probably okay since it's not *that* identifiable, but once you get down to city levels if becomes a lot more identifiable. Recording US states is probably okay, since it's a big country comparable to the EU, but for something like Ireland I'd rather not record the county – just \"Ireland\" is more than specific enough. So we'd need some special-fu logic there too instead of just \"record it all\".\r\n\r\nAnd for a lot of people splitting out various US states provides little value, and may even be undesirable. Not sure how to best manage this UI-wise.\r\n\r\nAll-in-all, it's not a \"oh, let me just do this in 2 hours\"-kind of feature if we want to do it right. As always, I'm happy to accept patches but I think it's unlikely I'll work on this in the short term.\r\n\r\n> Is there a way to at least get raw data in the meantime?\r\n\r\nThere is no \"raw data\" for this; it gets the location from the GeoIP DB based on the IP address, and the IP address is never stored. There is no way to get more specific information for past requests.",
      "author_association": "OWNER",
