      "created_at": "2020-09-03T03:14:23Z",
      "updated_at": "2020-09-03T03:14:23Z",
      "body": "Like I mentioned @gabrielgggg, I think City level is too fine-grained both for reasons of privacy and UX, but yeah, US state would be good. I think the easiest way forward for this would be to create a new GeoIP database based on the \"Cities\" version but groups the cities by US state. I looked at this a while ago, but the tooling for all of this is a bit meh: they got some Perl library for this which can be used for this, but I'm not super familiar with Perl so all in all a bit time-consuming to get right.",
