      "created_at": "2020-12-28T10:01:20Z",
      "updated_at": "2020-12-28T10:01:20Z",
      "body": "Alright, this is now added: it records the region for every location, e.g. US state, which can be viewed by clicking on a country in the chart. Since this information wasn't collected before today and we have no way to get it, it will be \"unknown\" for entries before today.\r\n\r\nBecause some people may not want to collect this detailed information like I said before, you can enable/disable this in the \"data collection\" section on the settings that I added a few days ago; it's enabled by default.\r\n\r\nThis issue is still open as there's one part left to do: I want to be able to add a new (optional) dashboard chart which shows the regions for a particular country, so you can just add \"View regions for US\"; this requires a bit of work on the dashboard settings screen and I'll finish that up later this week.\r\n\r\nAs I mentioned, the expanded \"City\" version of the database is much larger than the Country (>60M), so you need to use `-geodb GeoLite2-City.mmdb` if you want to use this in a self-hosted installation. I looked a bit at creating a custom version which includes Country + Region information but not \"City\" and some other stuff we don't use, but I couldn't really get the Perl library to work, so 🤷‍♂️ Maybe I'll try again later.",
      "author_association": "OWNER",
      "pin": null,
