      "created_at": "2021-03-31T15:49:23Z",
      "updated_at": "2021-03-31T15:49:23Z",
      "body": "You need to use the `-geodb` flag @cwmke – the countries\" database is built in the binary as it's small enough, but with ~35M the cities one is too large. I don't know which database Fedora ships, but if it's a mmdb file it should work. Otherwise you can download it for free from the Maxmind website.\r\n\r\nYou need to be using v2.0.0 for this by the way.",
      "author_association": "OWNER",
      "pin": null,
